# Guru card auto-draft

When the user provides a **solutions doc** (uploaded file, pasted content, PDF, or markdown) and asks to generalize or create a Guru card:

1. Run the **guru-card-generator** skill end-to-end
2. If **Guru MCP** (`user-Guru`) is connected, **always** create a draft via `guru_create_draft` unless the user says not to
3. Follow [guru-config.md](../skills/guru-card-generator/guru-config.md) for collection, title prefix, and post-draft steps

## Input sources

| Source | How to read |
|--------|-------------|
| Uploaded PDF / image | Read file directly |
| Pasted markdown/text | Use pasted content |
| Local `.md` file | Read file |
| Google Doc **link only** | Cannot fetch directly — ask user to export (PDF/DOCX), paste content, or upload screenshots |
| Google Doc **export** | Read downloaded PDF/DOCX |

## MCP draft workflow

1. `guru_search_documents` — check for duplicate cards (agentId in guru-config.md)
2. Generate generalized card per skill (Purpose, Problem, etc.)
3. Save local copy to `examples/<pattern-slug>/output-guru-card.md`
4. `guru_create_draft` with:
   - `title`: `WIP: {card title}`
   - `content`: card body (markdown sections; user may restyle in Guru)
5. Return draft link/ID and manual follow-up checklist (collection, images, publish)

## Do not skip

- Anonymization and product-accuracy checks from the skill
- Screenshot borders (`scripts/add-image-borders.py`) when UI walkthrough content exists
- Redact secrets in screenshots before border step
